{"title":"2025 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1:_Casework\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1: Casework</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(broken_down)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (broken down)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(more_broken_down)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (more broken down)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4:_Casework\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4: Casework</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~1:20)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~1:20)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution(Quick_and_Easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution(Quick and Easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_DDM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by DDM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(intuitive)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (intuitive)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Chinese_Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Chinese Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(1.5_Min_Explanation)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (1.5 Min Explanation)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Fast_and_Intuitive)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Fast and Intuitive)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_The_Beauty_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">17</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by The Beauty of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">18</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many isosceles triangles are there with positive area whose side lengths are all positive integers and whose longest side has length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78db23e86da8fe319c63bdb5eaf6d3fd8fefa17b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/7/e3753a4d26a3d8ee9cb2f0ac22823f3f3848ff81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}~2025\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}~2026\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}~3012\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}~3037\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}~4050$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"487\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1:_Casework\">Solution 1: Casework</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1: Casework\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>You can split the problem into two cases:<br />\nCase <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />: The two sides with equal length are both smaller than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78db23e86da8fe319c63bdb5eaf6d3fd8fefa17b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, which means that they range from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/4/764b059fd41cd1b6b1b0b4841681f7d9c0b2f789.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1013$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/7/e5711c8d31d3bc3119aba377c9bda0f9dfb14e4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2024$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/3/d83eeb9ab5890602a512b7735f593abec1dc6978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> such cases.<br />\nCase <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />: There are two sides of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78db23e86da8fe319c63bdb5eaf6d3fd8fefa17b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, so the last side must be in the range <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78db23e86da8fe319c63bdb5eaf6d3fd8fefa17b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78db23e86da8fe319c63bdb5eaf6d3fd8fefa17b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> such cases. Keep in mind, an equilateral triangle also counts as an isosceles triangle, since it has <b>at least</b> 2 sides of equal length.<br />\nTherefore, the total number of cases is (equilateral + isosceles) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/e/81e1c4c3c2590b5dc4885ecc81156c7c07ae99ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1012 + 2025 = \\boxed{\\text{(D) }3037}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"200\" height=\"30\" /><br />\n~cw, minor edit by sd\n</p><p>Side note not by the author: If you're unsure whether the equilateral triangle is a valid case, notice that the other answers are much farther away, as compared to only a one-off error from 3037, which would make 3037 still the best answer.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28broken_down.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(broken_down)\">Solution 2 (broken down)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (broken down)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose an isosceles triangle has sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/3/923ebcf48ae334de6fc2ef155ce1e6a57effa23e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, A, B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is the longest side and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/f/bef747a48a2a8d43c4841e12c89f2de2502a672e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> are positive integers.\n</p><p>By the triangle inequalities:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/b/6bbbe93a7405ce04ea8ded3168b1f5c3d4f9edf9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A + A &gt; B\\]\" width=\"87\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/b/d2b7e54bc6b7671840d91e567d4853fd219b85b2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A + B &gt; A \\implies B &gt; 0\\]\" width=\"185\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>---\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/d/a6dac97076f3291f580214549968cf5c4309db9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = 2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"76\" height=\"14\" /> (the longest side):\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/0/d50bb43eb4f1886a8035b368a5c3865fb3238802.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2025 + 2025 &gt; B \\implies B &lt; 4050\\]\" width=\"257\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>But also, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is the longest side, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/3/c4313a11295bffff8a92569e3815043d2b269d7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B &lt; 2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />. Therefore,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/1/3f15a90adf953677e6435b2f6b34aa6cb07346d9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[B = 1, 2, 3, \\ldots, 2024,\\]\" width=\"162\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/7/e5711c8d31d3bc3119aba377c9bda0f9dfb14e4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2024$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" /> triangles.\n</p><p>---\n</p><p>Now consider triangles with side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/4/2f48886b349e5443e0ac98733d60a4acbae24609.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B, B, 2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/3/c4313a11295bffff8a92569e3815043d2b269d7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B &lt; 2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Triangle inequality gives:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/4/d347fa09308983818a19619b9b01a68be06c1f8c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[B + B &gt; 2025 \\implies B &gt; 1012.5\\]\" width=\"249\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is an integer and less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78db23e86da8fe319c63bdb5eaf6d3fd8fefa17b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, the possible values are\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/e/bde0840da5610ecc2af2f592f010e33d780a82e8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[B = 1013, 1014, 1015, \\ldots, 2024,\\]\" width=\"244\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>which gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/3/d83eeb9ab5890602a512b7735f593abec1dc6978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> triangles.\n</p><p>---\n</p><p>Finally, don’t forget the case where all sides are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78db23e86da8fe319c63bdb5eaf6d3fd8fefa17b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> (equilateral, which also counts as isosceles by definition). So add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more triangle.\n</p><p>---\n</p><p>In total,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7034697ae88f9c9afb088f7eeb71d3fb5c0fff.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2024 + 1012 + 1 = \\boxed{3037}\\]\" width=\"198\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>triangles.\n</p><p>~yuvaG\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28more_broken_down.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(more_broken_down)\">Solution 3 (more broken down)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (more broken down)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To solve this question, we first must observe the following restrictions given by the problem -  \n1.) Be an isosceles triangle  \n2.) Positive integer side lengths (causing a positive area)  \n3.) Longest length is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78db23e86da8fe319c63bdb5eaf6d3fd8fefa17b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />  \n</p><p>To satisfy restrictions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we can denote the side lengths of a triangle that satisfies these restrictions as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/5/9152abbb1e491a000651292849fa09f78d967c3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, A, B,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are positive integers. This is possible as the triangle is restricted to be isosceles, meaning at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> equal length sides.\n</p><p>In any triangle with side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, the following inequalities (Triangle Inequality Theorem) must hold:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/3/0a3d989c0938abd083035fa434aa75b4d3474b65.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a + b &gt; c\\]\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" />  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/f/81faf2590ff435f24a6819ac192e63b6a9a02583.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a + c &gt; b\\]\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" />  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/3/513349439e7e98155a2b8c58beba005da2e65dcd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b + c &gt; a\\]\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, our satisfactory triangles must satisfy\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/b/6bbbe93a7405ce04ea8ded3168b1f5c3d4f9edf9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A + A &gt; B\\]\" width=\"87\" height=\"14\" />  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/1/6e1f50372b0f39d7ea7072bfb9cf13baa4238dc9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A + B &gt; A.\\]\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d5e1dcec8d17bb45319e0f27f2e15f99e5ebc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A &gt; 0, B &gt; 0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Now we can focus on restriction <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/0/93032f1ab8b685d84a767a2fde0d9006a464b5e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3.$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" /> Let us consider that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78db23e86da8fe319c63bdb5eaf6d3fd8fefa17b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is the longest side length).\n</p><p>Substituting for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> we can rewrite our inequalities as follows\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/c/e7c2156d7649cde2d8d2ca730faa62d56137f985.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2025 + 2025 &gt; B\\]\" width=\"132\" height=\"14\" />  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/1/f219ed66dd0bb01ae13cd364ee491b3a764d4d9b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2025 + B &gt; 2025\\]\" width=\"132\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/8/c184ad907203e82580288872adc399a2dd40b845.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B &gt; 0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Furthermore, we can solve this system of linear inequalities like this\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/4/43471c5bb19ce453a99c94c5ee9a75bac8bbd5fd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4050 &gt; B\\]\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/f/4cf5c89d447c56fb6578d0171bf50ebd9dc94a9a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[B &gt; 0\\]\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/7/ca79d1a8baf218fc939a31a55ca389be53201053.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0 &lt; B &lt; 4050\\]\" width=\"107\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>However, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to be the longest side length, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> must be less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78db23e86da8fe319c63bdb5eaf6d3fd8fefa17b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, the solutions are\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/2/2f2afd2e5a4b7bfbb6ddbbe43c8716a3a239880d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{integers in } 0 &lt; B &lt; 2025 \\implies 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, \\ldots, 2024\\]\" width=\"393\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>This creates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/7/e5711c8d31d3bc3119aba377c9bda0f9dfb14e4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2024$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" /> cases.\n</p><p>---\n</p><p>Now let’s consider that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is the longest side length and it is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78db23e86da8fe319c63bdb5eaf6d3fd8fefa17b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Substituting for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, we can rewrite our inequalities as follows\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/d/0dd42e96fbc71d6e26c87583f6a819568508f61e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A + A &gt; 2025\\]\" width=\"108\" height=\"14\" />  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/5/2252e64426dd8f98f0111adcd88591b8799d479c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A + 2025 &gt; A\\]\" width=\"109\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/f/a1f0b85b0ee75ecf092602122285ac84dcc60007.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A &gt; 0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Furthermore, we can solve this system of linear inequalities like this\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/4/fd48fcb088ba9f9799beafb08536b194ea496da9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2A &gt; 2025\\]\" width=\"81\" height=\"14\" />  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/4/5f4f0e06489fa39c9f498a8e76cb89f8918b37aa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0 &lt; 2025\\]\" width=\"68\" height=\"14\" /> (which can be ignored as it is always true)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/d/afde7ddebad5429fc21cdd76fa1d16e17188fb6c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A &gt; 1012.5\\]\" width=\"87\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>However, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to be the longest side length, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> must be less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78db23e86da8fe319c63bdb5eaf6d3fd8fefa17b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, the solutions are\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/a/45ad34dd5029389de05c6296d93b8712cd5f6062.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{integers in } 1012.5 &lt; A &lt; 2025 \\implies 1013, 1014, 1015, 1016, \\ldots, 2024\\]\" width=\"525\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>This creates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62fd75708cb65aef3af02ced91ad6da8e66c2186.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2024 - 1012 = 1012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"157\" height=\"15\" /> cases.\n</p><p>---\n</p><p>But! here is also a case of an isosceles triangle where all side lengths of the triangle are equal in length and congruent - this special isosceles is referred to as an equilateral triangle. We can denote the lengths of such a triangle as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/b/9ebfe17f2b318e218d039609a2dcf32cc4537389.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, A, A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" />. We need to assign the longest length to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, as it is the only place a length can be applied. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/d/a6dac97076f3291f580214549968cf5c4309db9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = 2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"76\" height=\"14\" />. We do not need to worry about the Triangle Inequality Theorem as any equilateral shape always satisfies it. For example,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/8/ff81f0ae2c35ed992341b516cb12f3cd9b5a1686.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A + A &gt; A, \\quad A + A &gt; A, \\quad A + A &gt; A\\]\" width=\"311\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> of the Triangle Inequality Theorem are all equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/5/0b55fe8fe57c75f6688d3eb366fc0944fbbafa44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>is always satisfied for any side length, assuming that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is a positive integer.\n</p><p>This creates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> case.\n</p><p>---\n</p><p>Adding together our cases,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/1/2114d4328ac12649b04b8c85e9e88459638a67ff.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2024 + 1012 + 1 = \\boxed{\\text{(D) }3037}.\\]\" width=\"232\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>This is a process called casework.\n</p><p><br />\n~ yuvaG (idk why i felt like going this in depth for question <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, but enjoy 😉)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4:_Casework\">Solution 4: Casework</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4: Casework\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are two cases. The first case is where the other two side lengths are the congruent side lengths and less than 2025, and the second one is where 2025 is one of the congruent side lengths.\n</p><p>Case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />: We let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the other side length in the triangle. By the triangle inequality, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/3/223363bfb3e3c68e661704204b29c6805781e12e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2a&gt;2025 \\text{ and } a&lt;2025,\\]\" width=\"190\" height=\"16\" /> so we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d547b69a8c6212007ab25876dd47b1beb0f378d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1012.5&lt;a&lt;2025,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"152\" height=\"17\" /> and since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> can be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/2/34221886a5f5e3cb610a50102ea34ec800447044.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1013,2014,...,2024,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"155\" height=\"17\" /> so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/3/d83eeb9ab5890602a512b7735f593abec1dc6978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> such cases.\n</p><p>Case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />: We let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> be the other side in the triangle, since 2025 is one of the congruent sides. Since 2025 is the largest side, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/3/cf36360cf6a9e30794dd7b69f57e6946b0b24d28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&lt;2025,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" /> so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/7/e5711c8d31d3bc3119aba377c9bda0f9dfb14e4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2024$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" /> solutions in this case.\n</p><p>However, there is also a case where the triangle is equilateral so we add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/d/6cdd1b53e5faf7a118222e4b7571d1e9afa0cf56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>So, the total number of triangles that are isosceles with largest side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78db23e86da8fe319c63bdb5eaf6d3fd8fefa17b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/1/9f1b0ee4d34133080ad73a42de2eeb504fa1b7f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1012+2024+1=\\boxed{3037}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"200\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~ gogogo2022\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_.28Logical.2C_Good_Editing.2C_.7E1:20.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~1:20)\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~1:20)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~1:20)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/Ts7dCnEnu6o\">https://www.youtube.com/shorts/Ts7dCnEnu6o</a>\n</p><p>~Ebai\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/LN5ofIcs1kY\">https://youtu.be/LN5ofIcs1kY</a>\n</p><p>~Thesmartgreekmathdude\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution.28Quick_and_Easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution(Quick_and_Easy)\">Video Solution(Quick and Easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution(Quick and Easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wuLelj-DR9o\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wuLelj-DR9o</a>\n~Sigma_Bob\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_DDM\">Video Solution by DDM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by DDM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/s6ZFcqpIWj4\">https://youtu.be/s6ZFcqpIWj4</a>\n</p><p>~piggydude\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28intuitive.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(intuitive)\">Video Solution (intuitive)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (intuitive)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/gKV_oUR36xY?si=7r2Sk-pOOBc8maal\">https://youtu.be/gKV_oUR36xY?si=7r2Sk-pOOBc8maal</a> - Continuum Math\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Chinese_Video_Solution\">Chinese Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Chinese Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1hV2uBtENi/\">https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1hV2uBtENi/</a>\n</p><p>~metrixgo\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.281.5_Min_Explanation.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(1.5_Min_Explanation)\">Video Solution (1.5 Min Explanation)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (1.5 Min Explanation)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/vbdz7WmVuJ4\">https://youtu.be/vbdz7WmVuJ4</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dAeyV60Hu5c\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dAeyV60Hu5c</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Fast_and_Intuitive.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Fast_and_Intuitive)\">Video Solution (Fast and Intuitive)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/P